==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*10 [[Those Guys]] spawn after 4 seconds<sup>120f</sup>, delay 0.67~3.33 seconds<sup>20f~100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 22.67~26.67 seconds<sup>680f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 14 seconds<sup>420f</sup>, delay 26.67~28.67 seconds<sup>800f~860f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~28.67 seconds<sup>400f~860f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Manic Jamiera Cat (Enemy)|Manic Jamiera Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.
**10 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
**3 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Because boss spawns on base hit, you should use the start of the stage to save up money while stacking up attackers on the field. Manic Jamiera has a somewhat low range, but he is immediately accompanied by several Shadow Boxer Ks that will rip apart the front line if you're not careful. Furthermore, he has a 25% chance to create a level 7 wave attack, which is enough to cripple if not outright kill your units if it was to be unleashed, so the less waves he creates, the better. If one has [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], this will not completely erase the threat of these waves, but it will help you a LOT. If you don't have Octopus Cat, then you should focus on sending as little meatshields as possible, or focus your lineup on Wave Immune Cats and meatshields. Money is very forgiving in this stage, as the Gories and Gory Darks spawn at a constant rate, supplying you with money. Keep chipping down Manic Jamiera, and eventually you will win.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]: As stated before, Octopus Cat can help out a lot because of its ability to completely nullify waves, however at level 30 he will only be able to take 1 hit from Manic Jamiera without dying, so if you do bring it, never stop summoning it.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: With his massive damage against Black ability and decent overall DPS, he will obliterate the Gory Darks and Doge Darks, quickly supplying you with more money. He is a bit slow, however, so keep an eye out for that when you decide to use him.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: A very powerful unit capable of surviving one Manic Jamiera attack at level 30, his pure DPS is enough to take out huge chunks of Manic Jamiera's hp at once.
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]]: Because of the amount of money you'll have in this stage, Cyborg Cat is useful as a general attacker that is extremely easy to stack. She'll be your main source of DPS if you do decide to bring her.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Especially with their money UP [[Talents|talent]], they can and will be very useful towards beating Manic Jamiera due to their insane damage per hit. However, they have a relatively slow attack rate, so don't rely on them being your only damage source.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Disposable unit with a solid DPS, even though there's no red enemies in the stage. He'll rush to the front and land an attack or two on Manic Jamiera before dying, which can and will slowly chip him down.
*[[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]]/[[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]]: Long range single attackers, a stack of them has an amazing amount of DPS and will decimate any peons, as well as do a huge amount damage to the boss overtime.
*[[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed UFO Cat]]: Very good anti-Traitless if you have him. Massive Damage will aid you in destroying Maniac Jamiera.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] that is a ranged [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] and/or has a [[Special Abilities|special ability]] against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] or [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies should do well here, below this will have more specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage.
*[[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] and [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] Exclusives: As always, they do extremely well here as they are all [[Immune to Waves|immune to Waves]]— except [[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Eclipsed]], however, the EPICFEST ones are all better against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies while being able to perform decently against traited enemies. [[Dark Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Mitama]] has very good [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control]] with her 100% [[Weaken|weaken]] and [[Slow|slow]], [[Dark Aegis Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Aegis Garu]] can stall Manic Jamiera Cat for ages, and the others have insane DPS against Traitless enemies, same applies to the UBERFEST ones.
*[[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Shishilan Pasalan]]: They have high DPS when [[Strengthen|strengthened]] and wave immunity, enabling them to help whittle down Manic Jamiera's high HP. Plus, due to Shishilan's high knockback count, they will rarely ever die.
*[[Anubis the Protector (Uber Rare Cat)|Anubis the Protector]]: His high DPS can shred Manic Jamiera and the peons. He will avoid the wave and slow if ever hit, just be careful with the Gories, as they can kill him easily.
*[[Sengoku Wargods Vajiras (Gacha Event)|Sengoku Wargods]] tend to perform well here for the most part, with units like [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Maeda Keiji]] serving as a Wave-immune Tank and [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Sanada Yukimura]] being a great suicide rusher/nuker against the Gory Dark waves; [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Oda Nobunaga]] freezes the Gories so [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] can hit them, while [[Takeda Shingen (Uber Rare Cat)|Takeda Shingen]], [[Uesugi Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|Uesugi Kenshin]], [[Imagawa Yoshimoto (Uber Rare Cat)|Imagawa Yoshimoto]], and [[Amakusa Shiro (Uber Rare Cat)|Amakusa Shiro]] act as Midranger/Backliners and deal with the Gory Darks just as well. The last mentioned four need protection from a [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] to consistently act their roles, however.
*More specific pulls from other gachas such as [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]], [[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|Guardian Gamereon]], [[Sweet Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Sweet Aphrodite]], [[Squirtgun Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Squirtgun Saki]], and [[Seashore Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Seashore Kai]] are good in their niche and use here; though their roles vary from Tankers to Nukers.
*[[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]] can be used here since he has a gargantuan amount of health, huge attack power, and wave blocker. He's relatively cheap for an Uber, coming in at 3,600, and with [[Manic Jamiera Cat (Enemy)|Manic Jamiera Cat]]'s 5 knockbacks, Cat Machine can likely get a hit off, doing huge damage.

